<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Arc4u.Dependency.Tool">
      <PrivateAssets>all</PrivateAssets>
      <IncludeAssets>runtime; build; native; contentfiles; analyzers; buildtransitive</IncludeAssets>
    </PackageReference>
    <PackageReference Include="Arc4u.MongoDB" />
    <PackageReference Include="MongoDB.Bson" />
    <PackageReference Include="MongoDB.Driver" />
    <PackageReference Include="SharpCompress" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!--
    Arc4u.MongoDB - which brings MongoDB.Driver and Arc4u.Dependency along with it - is installed by the CLI
    from the Infrastructure.MongoDB set in nugets.json, which registers its central version in
    Directory.Packages.props at the same time. It cannot be listed here: Central Package Management rejects a
    versionless reference to a package it has no PackageVersion for.

    SharpCompress comes from that same set and is deliberately referenced even though no code here calls it:
    MongoDB.Driver depends on a SharpCompress old enough to be flagged by NuGet audit, and the transitive
    version is what the restore would otherwise pick. The PackageVersion the set writes lifts every project in
    the solution to the patched version (they resolve it as CentralTransitive); this direct reference is what
    makes the pin visible in the project that actually drags the dependency in.

    The reference on CampusHub.Enrollment.Domain is added by the CLI as well. It is the only project
    reference this assembly is allowed to take - it is an outward adapter, so nothing but the Host references
    it back and every dependency arrow points inwards.
  -->


  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\CampusHub.Enrollment.Domain\CampusHub.Enrollment.Domain.csproj" />
    <!-- Public event contract written to the outbox. -->
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Sdks\CampusHub.Enrollment.IntegrationEvents\CampusHub.Enrollment.IntegrationEvents.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
